@startuml DQIMS_Activity_Issue_Creation_Assignment
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

title <size:16><b>DQIMS - Issue Creation & Assignment Activity Diagram</b></size>\n<size:12>Complete Workflow from Creation to Assignment</size>\n

|#E8F5E9|Reporter (HOD/Secretary)|
start
:Navigate to Issue Reporting Module;

:Click "Create New Issue" Button;

:Fill Issue Form:
- Title
- Description
- Category
- Severity
- Priority
- Data Source
- Affected Records
- Data Field
- Tags;

:Upload Attachments (optional);

:Click "Submit" Button;

|#E3F2FD|System|
:Receive Issue Creation Request;

:Validate JWT Token;

if (Token Valid & User Authorized?) then (no)
  :Return Error: Unauthorized;
  |Reporter (HOD/Secretary)|
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:Validate Form Data;

if (All Required Fields Present?) then (no)
  :Return Validation Errors;
  |Reporter (HOD/Secretary)|
  :Fix Validation Errors;
  :Resubmit Form;
  |System|
endif

:Begin Database Transaction;

:Generate Unique Issue Number;
note right: ISS-2026-NNNN format

:Query SLA Configuration by:
- Severity
- Category
- Department;

if (SLA Config Found?) then (yes)
  :Calculate SLA Due Date;
  :Set SLA Status = ON_TRACK;
else (no)
  :Use Default SLA (by severity);
  :Calculate Due Date;
endif

:Create Issue Record:
- status = OPEN
- reported_by = current user
- department_id = user's department
- created_at = now;

:Save Issue to Database;

if (Attachments Present?) then (yes)
  fork
    :Upload Files to Storage;
  fork again
    :Create Attachment Records;
  end fork
  :Link Attachments to Issue;
endif

:Create Issue History Entry:
"Issue created by [User Name]";

:Create Audit Log Entry:
- action = CREATE
- module = IssueReporting
- entity = Issue
- user = current user;

:Commit Transaction;

|#FFF3E0|Notification Service|
fork
  :Create Notification for Department HOD:
  "New issue ISS-XXXX-YYYY created";
fork again
  :Send Email to Department HOD;
end fork

|System|
:Return Success Response with:
- Issue ID
- Issue Number
- Created At
- SLA Due Date;

|Reporter (HOD/Secretary)|
:Display Success Message;

:Redirect to Issue Detail Page;

note left
  <b>Issue is now created</b>
  with status = OPEN
  waiting for assignment
end note

' ========== ASSIGNMENT WORKFLOW ==========

|#E8F5E9|HOD (Head of Department)|
:Receive Notification;

:View Department Issues List;

:Open Issue Detail Page;

:Review Issue Details;

:Click "Assign Issue" Button;

:Select Team Member from Department;

:Add Assignment Notes (optional);

:Click "Assign" Button;

|#E3F2FD|System|
:Receive Assignment Request;

:Validate:
- User is HOD or ADMIN
- Assignee is in same department
- Issue is not already assigned;

if (Validation Passed?) then (no)
  :Return Error: Cannot Assign;
  |HOD (Head of Department)|
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:Update Issue Record:
- assigned_to = selected member
- status = IN_PROGRESS (optional)
- updated_at = now;

:Create Issue History Entry:
"Assigned to [Member Name] by [HOD Name]";

:Create Audit Log Entry:
- action = ASSIGN
- old_value = null
- new_value = member ID;

|#FFF3E0|Notification Service|
fork
  :Create In-App Notification for Assigned Member;
fork again
  :Send Email to Assigned Member:
  "Issue ISS-XXXX-YYYY assigned to you";
end fork

|System|
:Return Success Response;

|HOD (Head of Department)|
:Display Success Message:
"Issue assigned successfully";

|#FCE4EC|Assigned Member|
:Receive Email Notification;

:Receive In-App Notification;

:Login to DQIMS;

:View "My Issues" Dashboard;

:See Newly Assigned Issue;

:Start Working on Issue;

stop

legend right
  <b>Activity Diagram Legend:</b>
  
  <b>Actors:</b>
  <back:#E8F5E9>  </back> Reporter (HOD/Secretary)
  <back:#E3F2FD>  </back> System
  <back:#FFF3E0>  </back> Notification Service
  <back:#FCE4EC>  </back> Assigned Member
  
  <b>Key Points:</b>
  • Auto-generates issue number
  • Calculates SLA based on severity
  • Creates audit trail
  • Sends notifications
  • Role-based assignment
endlegend

@enduml
